            <ArticleTitle>Lead poisoning in Gurkha soldiers in Hong Kong.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>336-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Investigation of an outbreak of lead-poisoning in 121 Gurkha soldiers showed that this was due to the contamination of chilli powder (cayenne pepper), a constituent of curry powder, with lead chromate. Comprehensive systems of food sampling are needed in developing communities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
